course: dictionary
lesson: 15050
title: Retreated: moving back to safety
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Retreated is the past tense of retreat, so it tells us something has already happened. Retreat means to move back or away, usually to get away from something frightening or too strong to face. «The cat retreated under the sofa when the dog barked.» The cat went back, away from the dog, to feel safe.
explain: Context gives you the clue. Look at what happens before and after the word. If there is danger, an enemy, or a wish to be alone, retreated probably means moved back to a safer place. Then try the swap: "The cat moved back to a safer place under the sofa" still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Retreated can also mean changing a decision. «The coach retreated from his plan when the players complained.» Nobody moved anywhere; the coach stepped back from his idea because of the pressure. Ice can retreat too: «The glacier retreated up the valley as the weather grew warmer.»
fact: Retreat is the base word; retreated is the past tense, and retreating is the -ing form.
fact: «Retreated» means moved back or away, especially from danger or an enemy.
fact: «Retreated» can also mean went to a quiet, safe place, as in «She retreated to her room to read.»
fact: «Retreated» can mean changed a plan because of pressure. «Beat a retreat» means to leave or go back.
fact: A glacier is a huge, slow river of ice. When it retreats, it shrinks back up the valley.
exercise: «After losing the battle, the army retreated over the river.» What does retreated mean here? | *Moved back, away from the enemy | Fell asleep on the bank | Charged forward at full speed | Stayed and built a bridge
exercise: «Tired of the noise, Maya retreated to her quiet bedroom.» Which phrase tells you where Maya went? | The middle of the busy road | *A quiet, safe place | A loud party in the garden | The top of a tall tree
exercise: Find and copy the word from this sentence that means went back: «The glacier retreated slowly as the valley grew warmer.» | glacier | slowly | *retreated | valley
test: «The coach retreated from his plan when the players complained.» What does retreated mean here? | Painted the goal posts | Ran away from the football pitch | *Changed a plan because of pressure | Bought new boots for the team
test: Which sentence uses retreated to mean that ice went back? | The glacier was painted bright blue for the show. | *The glacier retreated up the valley each year. | The glacier made a sound like thunder. | The glacier raced down the hill in a loud rush.
exam: What does the phrase «beat a retreat» most likely mean? | To dance in a long line | *To leave or go back | To win a game with a big drum | To sing very loudly
